`$self->{headers}{lc $name}` is an array ref of array refs, where each inner array ref is `[$name, $value]` representing one header line.

Given the signature `$headers->add(Foo => 'first value', 'second value')` adds two lines, each value becomes a separate header line:

```perl
sub add {
  my ($self, $name) = (shift, shift);

