Looking at other methods like `header` (which sets/replaces) and `every_header` (which returns all values), and the internal storage pattern in Mojo::Headers, headers are stored in `$self->{headers}` as an array reference of `[name, value]` pairs, with a case-insensitive lookup via a normalized name.

Based on the Mojo::Headers source code patterns, the internal structure uses:
- `$self->{headers}` - an array ref of `[$name, $value]` pairs
- `$self->{normalcase}` - mapping from lowercase name to original case

