1. **Setter mode**: Takes a hashref like `{next => 'http://example.com/foo', prev => 'http://example.com/bar'}` and sets the `Link` header accordingly in RFC 5988 format.
2. **Getter mode**: Parses the `Link` header and returns a hashref where keys are `rel` values, and values are hashrefs containing `link` and any other parameters (like `title`).

The Link header format per RFC 5988 is like: `<http://example.com/foo>; rel="next", <http://example.com/bar>; rel="prev"; title="Bar"`

I can use the `header_params` utility from `Mojo::Util` to parse the parameters after the URL portion.

