Wait, there's a problem. The file has `use integer;` which means all arithmetic will be integer arithmetic. Division would be integer division, losing the decimal parts needed for `_round` to work properly (e.g., "7.5GiB").

Let me reconsider. With `use integer` in effect, I need to use `no integer` within the function to get floating-point division.

```perl
sub humanize_bytes {
  my $size = shift;

  no integer;

  my $sign = $size < 0 ? '-' : '';
  $size = abs $size;

  # Bytes
  return "${sign}${size}B" if $size < 1024;

  # KiB
  my $k = $size / 1024;
  return $sign . _round($k) . 'KiB' if $k < 1024;

  # MiB
  my $m = $k / 1024;
  return $sign . _round($m) . 'MiB' if $m < 1024;

  # GiB
  my $g = $m / 1024;
  return $sign . _round($g) . 'GiB' if $g < 1024;

  # TiB
  my $t = $g / 1024;
  return $sign . _round($t) . 'TiB';
}
```

