Hmm, but the transaction's `send` already sets up drain and calls resume. Let me look again at `Mojo::Transaction::WebSocket::send`:

```perl
sub send {
  my ($self, $msg, $cb) = @_;
  $self->once(drain => $cb) if $cb;
  $msg = $self->build_message($msg) unless ref $msg eq 'ARRAY';
  $self->{write} .= Mojo::WebSocket::build_frame($self->masked, @$msg);
  return $self->emit('resume');
}
```

So I should NOT pass the callback to `$tx->send`, but instead set it up myself with the controller wrapper. And I should call `$tx->send($msg)` without the callback:

```perl
sub send {
  my ($self, $msg, $cb) = @_;

  my $tx = $self->tx;

  Carp::croak 'No WebSocket connection to send message to' unless $tx->is_websocket;

  $self->rendered(101) unless $tx->established;

  $tx->once(drain => sub { $self->$cb }) if $cb;
  $tx->send($msg);

  return $self;
